.\" nostr-dispatcher(1) — nostrc-prqu.7
.TH NOSTR-DISPATCHER 1 "2026-09-26" "nostrc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-dispatcher \- open nostr: links in the application registered for the event kind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-dispatcher open
.IR URI | FILE
.br
.B nostr-dispatcher resolve
.I URI
.br
.B nostr-dispatcher query-default
.IR KIND | *
.br
.B nostr-dispatcher set-default
.IR KIND | A-B | *
.I DESKTOP-ID
.br
.B nostr-dispatcher daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-dispatcher
is the sole desktop handler for
.BR x-scheme-handler/nostr ,
.B x-scheme-handler/web+nostr
and
.B application/vnd.nostr.event+json
files.
It parses a NIP-21
.B nostr:
link (or a bare NIP-19 identifier), learns the event kind (from the
.B naddr
or
.B nevent
TLV, or by fetching the event from the per-user session relay and then
the link's relay hints), and hands the link to the application registered
for that kind.
Links carrying a secret key
.RB ( nsec1 ,
.BR ncryptsec1 )
are refused.
.PP
Applications declare the kinds they handle with
.B X-Nostr-Kinds=
in their desktop entry; the user overrides the choice in
.IR handlers.list .
The URI handed to an application is always the dispatcher's canonical
re-encoding, never the caller's raw string.
.PP
When the chosen application is already running and implements
.B org.nostr.Handler2
(or the older
.BR org.nostr.Handler1 ),
the validated event is delivered over D-Bus instead of launching a
second instance.
Otherwise the application is launched from its desktop entry (argv, no
shell) and moved into its own transient
.B app-nostr\ex2ddispatcher-\fIAPP\fB-\fIPID\fB.scope
on the systemd user manager, like applications started from the shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI open " URI" | FILE
Dispatch a link or an event file.
Links are forwarded to the
.B org.nostr.Dispatcher1
service (D-Bus activated) and handled in-process only when no session bus
or service is available.
Event files are always handled in-process.
Prints the chosen desktop id on standard output.
.TP
.BI resolve " URI"
Dry run: print
.I kind
TAB
.I desktop-id
TAB
.I source
without launching anything.
.TP
.BI query-default " KIND" | *
Print the handler for a kind
.RB ( *
= the generic fallback viewer) and where the choice came from.
.TP
.BI set-default " KEY DESKTOP-ID"
Write
.I KEY=DESKTOP-ID;
into the
.B [Default Handlers]
group of the user's
.IR handlers.list .
.I KEY
is a kind, an inclusive range
.IR A-B ,
or
.BR * .
.TP
.B daemon
Run the
.B org.nostr.Dispatcher1
service (normally started by D-Bus activation through
.BR nostr-dispatcher.service ;
exits after 30 s idle).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nostr/handlers.list
User choices; highest precedence.
.TP
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/nostr/handlers.list ", " $XDG_DATA_DIRS/nostr/handlers.list
System and vendor defaults.
.PP
.I handlers.list
is a key file with the groups
.B [Default Handlers]
(kind token = ';'-separated desktop ids, first installed one wins),
.B [Removed Handlers]
(hide an application's
.B X-Nostr-Kinds
claim for some kinds) and
.BR [Dispatcher] ,
whose
.B fetch-relay-hints=false
stops the dispatcher from contacting relays named in links.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nostr/relay.sock
The per-user session relay, asked first for events.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_ACTIVATION_TOKEN ", " DESKTOP_STARTUP_ID
Forwarded to the launched application, or passed as
.B activation-token
in
.BR org.nostr.Handler2 's
platform data.
.TP
.B NOSTR_DISPATCHER_NO_DBUS=1
Always dispatch in-process.
.TP
.B NOSTR_DISPATCHER_NO_SCOPE=1
Do not move launched applications into their own systemd scope.
.TP
.B NOSTR_LOG_LEVEL=debug
Show libnostr's relay wire traces on standard error (quiet by default).
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=nostr-dispatcher
Show the dispatcher's own debug messages.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the link cannot be opened (invalid, forbidden, not
found, no handler, launch failure), 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR systemd.scope (5)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/nostr-dispatcher/README.md
and the D-Bus interfaces in
.IR /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/org.nostr.{Dispatcher1,Handler1,Handler2}.xml .
